{"seq":18,"trial_id":"harness-zero-select-2026-11/zero-full-no-scoped-notes-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T22:16:44.424Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"165026eeeb3c0337947073478acd2202e537da37d0fa3d26d815b94638489135","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes:\n\n1. **#PD-4492.** Source: \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting their SMS bay assignments. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the 04:00 shift got through the gate without help.\n2. **#4419.** Source: \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it went to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nThings to know before you paste these in:\n- The two numbers are formatted differently, and both involve Door 14 at the gatehouse. They may or may not be related. Nothing I found links them, and #4419 has no date.\n- Moss's other notes either don't mention Quarrendon or mention it without a ticket number: the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest, the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in and the Central digests. The Central tickets (#4409, #4412 and FR-882) belong to Marrow accounts, not Quarrendon.\n- Watch out for \"Quarendon Freightways\" (one R). It's a different company, not a customer, and it only appears in Marcus's competitor note, not in Moss's.\n\nI only looked at Moss's notes that you can see yourself, which are the team digests. If Moss has private notes, they aren't included here."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
